  "findings": [
    "Dropping unjudged rows collapses retrieval: both runs score 26-29% Hit@10 versus 56.00%, about cosine-only level.",
    "The judged negatives were selected for high retrieval scores, so within those rows high scores no longer separate references; the model never sees the ~210 ordinary messages per question it must rank at inference.",
    "Qwen useful labels help: graded beats control at all 27 tree settings, by +3.22 points Hit@10 on average (+0.83 to +4.96) and +1.42 NDCG@10."
  ],
  "decision": "Do not adopt either model. Keep the current model; test Qwen labels on all rows (unjudged = 0) next."
}
